/**
 * Constellation of live SVG dashboards around the hero composer.
 *
 * Decorative only (`aria-hidden`). Hero.astro assigns four of these to the
 * corner slots and marks the one that matches the cycling prompt. Eight live
 * in the DOM so the world atlas has more than two instruments.
 *
 * Every screen is drawn to read as a real instrument, not an illustration:
 * the world map is a coastline landmask rendered as dotted strokes, the mesh
 * viewer projects an actual subdivided icosahedron, the math lab integrates
 * the Lorenz system at build time, the radar sweep lights each contact as it
 * passes its bearing. All geometry is computed in the frontmatter so the
 * client ships only static SVG plus CSS keyframes — no runtime JS.
 *
 * Colours come from the world surface tokens, so the boards follow the page
 * theme without per-scene overrides.
 */
